<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> politician, prime minister from 1960 to 1964 and president of the Somali Republic from 1967. His governments pursued the union of all Somali-inhabited lands, backing insurgents in Kenya's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-frontier-district">Northern Frontier District</a>. He was assassinated by one of his bodyguards on 15 October 1969, and six days later the army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Siad Barre</a> seized power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke.jpg" alt="Abdirashid Ali Shermarke" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Somalia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdirashid_Ali_Shermarke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
